      "itemDescription": "Sysco, a food marketer and distributor, jumped up 14 spots on the Fortune 500 and posted a 34% increase in revenue in 2022, as restaurant demand\u2014abnormally low during the height of the pandemic\u2014rebounded.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>The majority of Sysco's sales come from operations in the U.S., but international growth outstripped domestic in 2022, partly due to the reversal of more stringent pandemic restrictions abroad.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company sued a slew of meat companies in 2022, alleging that they violated antitrust regulations through price fixing. Although Sysco moved to settle the lawsuits, it is now mired in a legal battle with Burford Capital, which financed Sysco\u2019s litigation.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The workforce for the food marketer and distributor grew 22% in size from 2021, the third largest increase among the top 100 companies in the Fortune 500.</li><br />\r\n</ul>",
      "uri": "/ranking/fortune500/2023/",
      "__typename": "_ItemRankingListsType"
    },
